# Visual Go/No-Go EEG

Worked example accompanying the eeg-bids-converter skill. One participant, one
run, shortened to keep the example small. Not real data.

## What was recorded

64-channel EEG plus two EOG channels, sampled at 500 Hz, during a visual
Go/No-Go task. Participants pressed the space bar for Go stimuli and withheld
the response for No-Go stimuli.

## Known issues

Channel T7 was noisy throughout and is marked `bad` in `channels.tsv`.

## Provenance

Source archive: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.0000000
Converted with the eeg-bids-converter skill. `EEGGround` was not stated in the
source documentation and is recorded as "n/a" rather than guessed.
